{"url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/cc/programmes/research-degree-programmes/admission-overview", "final_url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/cc/programmes/research-degree-programmes/admission-overview", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-18", "text": "Home\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nResearch\nGlobal Outreach\nStudent Life & Learning\nDistinguished Seminar Series\nNews & Events\nQuick Links\nAdmission Overview\nHome Programmes Research Degree Programmes Admission Overview\nUndergraduate Programmes\nFlagship Programme\nJoint Bachelor's Degree Programmes\nMaster's Programmes\nResearch Degree Programmes\nAdmission Overview\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme\nAdmission\nEligibility\nMaster of Philosophy (MPhil):\nhold a relevant bachelor's degree with first or second class honours (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university.\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD):\nhold a higher degree by research (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university;\nor\nbe a current MPhil student in the University who is seeking transfer to PhD candidature;\nor\nhold a Master's degree (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university;\nor\nhold a Bachelor's degree with first class honours (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university.\nEquivalent qualifications mentioned above include relevant professional qualifications or other scholarly achievements recognised by the University.\nEnglish Proficiency Requirements\na minimum TOEFL total score of 79 (for tests taken prior to 21 January 2026) or 4.5 (for tests taken from 21 January 2026 onwards) (Internet-based test)*;\nor\na minimum overall band score of 6.5 in IELTS*;\nor\nother test scores that may be regarded as equivalent to TOEFL 79 (Internet-based test);\nor\na minimum score of 490 in the Chinese mainland\u2019s College English Test Band 6 may be accepted.\n*TOEFL and IELTS scores are considered valid for two years from the test date and must be valid at the time of submission of application.\nCollege English Test (CET) is NOT accepted as an equivalent English proficiency test for Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS). For applicants with strong academic and research potential who have only taken CET-6 with a minimum score of 490, special consideration may be made on a case-by-case basis during normal round admission.\nProgramme List\nOffering Unit Programme Title\nDepartment of Biostatistics Master of Philosophy (MPhil) /\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Biostatistics\nDepartment of Computer Science Master of Philosophy (MPhil) /\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Computer Science\nDepartment of Data Science Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Data Science\nApply now to embark on your journey! Apply Now\nFinancial Aid\nAdmitted students will receive the university scholarship with a monthly stipend of HK$19,100 (US$2,433) during their PhD studies at CityUHK. (Applicable to government-funded students only)\nOutstanding candidates will be recommended for the Hong Kong PhD Fellowship with a monthly stipend of HK$28,700 (US$3,680); during their PhD studies at CityUHK.\nFor the full list of scholarships and financial aid, please visit www.cityu.edu.hk/pg/research-degree-programmes/scholarships-financial-aid-and-fees.\nProgramme Details & Admission\nPlease visit SGS website for programme details & admission or contact the Departmental Research Degree Coordinators.\nResearch Degree Coordinators\nDepartment of Biostatistics\nProf. XU Jinfeng\nTel: (852) 3442 4183\nEmail: jinfenxu@cityu.edu.hk\nDepartment of Computer Science\nProf. ZHANG Qingfu\nTel: (852) 3442 8580\nEmail: qingfu.zhang@cityu.edu.hk\nDepartment of Data Science\nProf. WU Qi\nTel: (852) 3442 7018\nEmail: qi.wu@cityu.edu.hk\nAbout Us\nVision & Mission\nMessage from the Dean\nOur Rankings\nAbout the College\nManagement Team\nRecognitions\nContact Us\nProgrammes\nUndergraduate Programmes\nFlagship Programme\nJoint Bachelor's Degree Programmes\nMaster's Programmes\nResearch Degree Programmes\nResearc